<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        THE APPROVAL AUTO-ADVANCE SEMAPHORE (design decision D-1). SYSTEM-WRITTEN ONLY.

        WHAT WRITES IT: the workflow field update Set_Approval_Advance_Pending
        (workflows/Disposition__c.workflow-meta.xml), fired as a finalApprovalActions entry by
        THREE approval processes on this object: Sale_Decision_Approval,
        Broker_Selection_Approval and Closing_Approval. It only ever writes TRUE.

        WHAT CLEARS IT: DispositionApprovalAdvanceQueueable, in the same DML that writes the
        new stage. Nothing else clears it.

        WHY A SEMAPHORE INSTEAD OF THE APPROVAL WRITING Disposition_Stage__c DIRECTLY. Two
        mechanisms were rejected, and both rejections are recorded elsewhere in this repo:
          1. A DIRECT STAGE FieldUpdate BYPASSES VALIDATION RULES ENTIRELY. That is the
             reasoning already carried in Wire_Complete_Before_Completed's XML comment and in
             all three approval descriptions. An approval that skipped the all-NDAs-signed gate
             or the wire gate would be a hole in exactly the controls those rules exist for.
          2. AN APPROVAL-TRIGGERED FLOW RUNS AS THE APPROVER. A record-triggered flow with no
             runInMode fires in USER context, so the DML lands on the approver's CRUD, not the
             submitter's. That is a measured incident on this org, not a theory.
        The semaphore re-fires DispositionTrigger; the after-update handler detects false to
        true and enqueues a Queueable that writes the stage with ordinary
        Database.update(..., false, AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE). Validation rules still evaluate,
        approver CRUD is irrelevant, and the recordEditability = AdminOnly lock has definitively
        released by the time the job runs.

        🔴 THIS FIELD DELIBERATELY HAS NO FIELD-LEVEL SECURITY IN ANY PERMISSION SET, AND THAT
        IS NOT AN OVERSIGHT TO "FIX". A Metadata-API-deployed custom field arrives with no FLS
        for any profile, System Administrator included, and it is left that way here: nothing in
        the UI reads it, no layout carries it, and no flexipage visibility rule tests it. Every
        writer and reader is either a workflow field update or Apex in SYSTEM mode, neither of
        which consults FLS. Adding a grant would put a machine flag on a user's screen and
        invite a hand-edit that would fire a spurious stage advance.
        ⚠ THE COROLLARY: this field is INVISIBLE IN THE UI, including to an admin debugging a
        stuck record. Query it (SOQL / the developer console) rather than looking for it on the
        page. If an advance fails, the flag is LEFT TRUE on purpose so that query finds it.

        ⚠ IT IS AN INTERLOCK, NOT AN AUDIT TRAIL. It records only that an advance is OWED, never
        which approval owed it. The Queueable derives the target from (record type, current
        stage), so the same flag serves all three processes; approval history is where "who
        approved what" lives.

        =====================================================================================
        ADDED 2026-08-21 (ADDITIVE POINTER ONLY. NOTHING ABOVE THIS LINE IS RETRACTED OR
        CHANGED; every sentence above still holds.)
        =====================================================================================
        🔴 A SECOND, SIMILARLY NAMED FIELD NOW EXISTS ON THIS OBJECT:
        Disposition__c.Approval_Pending__c. DO NOT CONFLATE THEM, and do not wire one to the
        other's readers. They are opposites in time and have opposite FLS decisions:

            THIS FIELD  Approval_Advance_Pending__c   true on FINAL APPROVAL   NO FLS anywhere
            THAT FIELD  Approval_Pending__c           true while PENDING       read FLS in the
                                                                               two Disposition
                                                                               permission sets

        THAT field is a UI flag: four Dynamic Actions on Disposition_Record_Page hide their
        Submit button while it is true, which is exactly why it needs read FLS and this one must
        never be granted any. Read its XML comment before touching either.

        ⚠ AND THE THREE REASONS THIS FIELD COULD NOT SIMPLY BE REUSED FOR THAT JOB ARE WORTH
        RECORDING HERE, because reuse is the obvious first idea: it fires on the wrong EVENT
        (approval, not submission); it has no FLS by explicit decision above, and a visibility
        rule reading an unreadable field evaluates FALSE, which would have hidden all four
        buttons for everyone; and the paragraph above deliberately LEAVES IT TRUE on a failed
        advance, which would have hidden a Submit button permanently on exactly the records that
        most need it.
    -->
    <fullName>Approval_Advance_Pending__c</fullName>
    <defaultValue>false</defaultValue>
    <description>SYSTEM FIELD - DO NOT HAND-EDIT, AND DO NOT GRANT FLS. Set true by the Set_Approval_Advance_Pending field update on final approval of Sale Decision, Broker Selection or Closing. DispositionApprovalAdvanceQueueable reads it, writes the next stage and clears it. Left true on a failed advance so the stuck record is findable. See the XML comment in this file.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Internal interlock used by the approval auto-advance job. It is not shown on any page and must not be edited by hand.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Approval Advance Pending</label>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Checkbox</type>
</CustomField>
